cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research software, please cite this repository and the original methods identified in the README."
type: software
title: "Evolving Adaptive Collective Search: LLM Program Evolution for Dynamic Multi-Swarm Optimization"
authors:
  - family-names: "Löchli"
    given-names: "Roland"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ReloadLightly/shinka-adaptive-swarms"
url: "https://github.com/ReloadLightly/shinka-adaptive-swarms"
abstract: >-
  Research software studying whether native ShinkaEvolve program evolution can
  improve adaptation in dynamic multi-swarm particle swarm optimization. The
  project reconstructs a literature-based baseline from DEAP and evaluates
  evolved adaptation programs on the Moving Peaks Benchmark.
keywords:
  - program evolution
  - ShinkaEvolve
  - swarm intelligence
  - particle swarm optimization
  - dynamic optimization
  - reproducible research
